WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.867
Doing more work does not automatically produce improvement.

00:00:02.867 --> 00:00:07.017
A person can handle many tickets, attend many meetings, resolve many incidents,

00:00:07.017 --> 00:00:10.476
or complete many projects and still repeat the same mistakes.

00:00:10.476 --> 00:00:13.589
Learning requires feedback, attention, comparison, correction, and changed behavior.

00:00:13.589 --> 00:00:17.048
Experience creates exposure, but exposure alone does not guarantee skill.

00:00:17.048 --> 00:00:20.161
Repeated mistakes often persist because assumptions are not examined.

00:00:20.161 --> 00:00:23.273
A team may assume a user understands a workflow,

00:00:23.273 --> 00:00:27.424
a developer may assume a failure is caused by the newest change,

00:00:27.424 --> 00:00:30.191
or a leader may assume silence means agreement.

00:00:30.191 --> 00:00:33.650
If those assumptions are never surfaced, the same pattern returns.

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:37.108
The event changes, but the mental model remains the same.

00:00:37.108 --> 00:00:41.259
Busy environments often skip learning because the next demand arrives before the

00:00:41.259 --> 00:00:42.988
current one has been understood.

00:00:42.988 --> 00:00:47.139
After a release, incident, review, or customer escalation, people move on quickly.

00:00:47.139 --> 00:00:49.214
That feels efficient in the moment,

00:00:49.214 --> 00:00:52.327
but it can create false confidence or shallow conclusions.

00:00:52.327 --> 00:00:57.169
A quick story about what happened may replace a careful look at the evidence.

00:00:57.169 --> 00:00:59.244
Reflective practice turns events into evidence.

00:00:59.244 --> 00:01:02.357
It connects actions, decisions, outcomes, context, and future changes.

00:01:02.357 --> 00:01:05.816
Instead of asking only whether something went well or badly,

00:01:05.816 --> 00:01:09.274
it asks why the result happened, what signals were missed,

00:01:09.274 --> 00:01:12.387
what constraints shaped the decision, what feedback was available,

00:01:12.387 --> 00:01:15.846
and what specific adjustment would make the next attempt stronger.

00:01:15.846 --> 00:01:21.380
This is how a busy person protects learning from being washed away by the next task.
